  "problem": {
    "id": "train-720",
    "question": "Mr. Callen bought 10 paintings at $40 each and 8 wooden toys at $20 each from the crafts store to resell at a profit. However, when he sold the items, the selling price of a painting was 10% less and the selling price of a hat 15% less. Calculate the total loss Mr. Callen made from the sale of the items.",
    "gold": "64",
    "answer": "If he sold a painting at a 10% loss, then he made a 10/100*$40 = $<<10/100*40=4>>4 loss on each painting.\nsince he bought 10 paintings, the total loss he made from selling the paintings is 10*$4 = $<<10*4=40>>40\nHe also made a loss of 15/100*20 = $<<15/100*20=3>>3 loss from selling each wooden toy.\nSince he bought 8 wooden toys, the total loss he made was 3*8 = $<<8*3=24>>24\nIn total, Mr. Callen made a loss of $40+$24 = $<<40+24=64>>64 from the sales of the items.\n#### 64"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total loss Mr. Callen made from the sale of the items, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total cost of the paintings and wooden toys.\n2. Determine the selling price of each painting and each wooden toy.\n3. Calculate the total revenue from selling the paintings and wooden toys.\n4. Find the total loss by subtracting the total revenue from the total cost.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total cost of the paintings and wooden toys.**\n\nThe cost of 10 paintings at $40 each is:\n\\[ 10 \\times 40 = 400 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThe cost of 8 wooden toys at $20 each is:\n\\[ 8 \\times 20 = 160 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThe total cost is:\n\\[ 400 + 160 = 560 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\n**Step 2: Determine the selling price of each painting and each wooden toy.**\n\nThe selling price of a painting is 10% less than the cost price of $40:\n\\[ 40 \\times (1 - 0.10) = 40 \\times 0.90 = 36 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThe selling price of a wooden toy is 15% less than the cost price of $20:\n\\[ 20 \\times (1 - 0.15) = 20 \\times 0.85 = 17 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the total revenue from selling the paintings and wooden toys.**\n\nThe revenue from selling 10 paintings at $36 each is:\n\\[ 10 \\times 36 = 360 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThe revenue from selling 8 wooden toys at $17 each is:\n\\[ 8 \\times 17 = 136 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThe total revenue is:\n\\[ 360 + 136 = 496 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\n**Step 4: Find the total loss by subtracting the total revenue from the total cost.**\n\nThe total loss is:\n\\[ 560 - 496 = 64 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThus, the total loss Mr. Callen made from the sale of the items is:\n\\[ \\boxed{64} \\]",
